# Evidence directories are written at run time by examples and must never be committed.
# (See examples/README.md — the `evidence/` convention.)
**/evidence/
# Some examples emit a SECOND report for a distinct measurement mode, so it can stand beside the first
# rather than overwrite it. In iot-timeseries, `evidence/` is the PRIMARY report — the file-backed run
# against a real server, which carries the durable-byte evidence — and `evidence-mirror/` is the
# deterministic in-memory CONTROL beside it. (Before `rmp` #713 those roles were inverted: the simulator
# was the headline and the real server's report was a side file nothing gated. The rename is the fix.)
# Same rule: generated at run time, never committed.
**/evidence-mirror/

# Python bytecode caches from the REST example's generator (never source, never evidence).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
